---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="About | Joe Fazio"
  description="Joe Fazio: recent Computer Information Systems graduate looking for work across IT."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="intro">
    <Image
      class="portrait"
      src={headshot}
      alt="Joe Fazio."
      widths={[260, 520]}
      sizes="(max-width: 34rem) 45vw, 13rem"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <div>
      <p>
        I'm Joe. I graduated from James Madison University with a degree in
        Computer Information Systems, taken through the College of Business,
        which mostly meant learning to ask what a system is <em>for</em> before
        arguing about how to build it.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm looking for work across IT: help desk, systems administration, cloud
        support, IT analyst, junior security. That is a wide net and it is
        deliberate. I would rather land somewhere I can be useful early than pick
        a title now and pretend I have been walking toward it the whole time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The two things worth knowing about how I work: I am reliable and I am
    persistent. I finish what I pick up, and I stay on a problem past the point
    where it stops being interesting.
  </p>

  <h2>What I'm building</h2>

  <p>
    This site. The infrastructure is the point: Astro, Cloudflare Pages, DNS I
    manage myself, and a build in GitHub Actions that has to pass before anything
    reaches the main branch. The repository is public and every choice in it has
    a written reason attached, including the ones I got wrong and went back to
    fix. I wanted infrastructure I could explain out loud rather than a template
    I clicked into existence.
  </p>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .intro > div {
    flex: 1 1 18rem;
  }

  .intro p:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .portrait {
    flex: 0 0 13rem;
    width: 13rem;
    max-width: 45%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 5px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22);
  }

  @media (max-width: 26rem) {
    .portrait {
      max-width: 60%;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
  }
</style>
